🔹 🎯 Task: Read Configuration Using Java Properties
You are building a small app that loads settings from a .properties file.
📥 Input:
File: app.properties
Keys:
app.name=MyApp
app.version=1.0
app.debug=true
⚙️ Requirements:
• Create a app.properties file with the keys above
• Load the file using the Java Properties API
• Read each key and print:
"Name: <app.name>"
"Version: <app.version>"
"Debug: <app.debug>"
• If a key is missing, print a default value:
Name → "Unknown"
Version → "0.0"
Debug → "false"
📌 Constraints:
• Use only standard Java
• Output must match the required format exactly
📤 Output format:
Name: <value>
Version: <value>
Debug: <value></value></value></value>
📌 Test cases:
Input file:
app.name=MyApp
app.version=1.0
app.debug=true
Output:
Name: MyApp
Version: 1.0
Debug: true
Input file (missing app.version):
app.name=MyApp
app.debug=true
Output:
Name: MyApp
Version: 0.0
Debug: true